description: Follow-up from the review of #76 (D234). Records now have ckind 45, and `sortable?` in rt/wasm/core.lg has no arm for it, so `(sort r)` and `(sort-by f r)` on a record raise "sort expected a Collection" where native lg sorts the entries. `sort*` already goes through `sq/vec`, which handles records, so the fix is a `(= k 45) true` arm.
 
 Facts that close it
 F1 `sortable?` accepts kind 45: rt/wasm/core.lg, the `sortable?` cond.
 F2 a corpus case sorts a record with `sort` and with `sort-by` and matches native: `checks/oracle.sh corpus/wasm/records.lg` exits 0.

